        "date": "2026-11-16T00:05:43Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools)!: a tool's library holder is a reference to the entry\n\nA tool that sits in a built-in library holder stores the entry's name,\nthe gauge length and the projection (HolderRef on ToolBody::library),\nnot a drawn copy of the outline. tool_body::build_library is the one\nplace a reference becomes a shape: the SetToolBody / AddTool command,\nthe project loader and the .camtools reader call it, so the collision\nlaws, the stamp, the simulation and the preview read one body.\n\n- Project (v62) and .camtools (version 2 when a tool names a library\n  holder) write `holder: {entry, gauge_len, projection}` in place of\n  `body`.\n- An older file is not rewritten: a drawn copy of a library holder and\n  a holder_d/holder_len cylinder load as the custom holder they were.\n- A name the library does not hold, a grouped pick, lengths the entry\n  cannot take, or `holder` beside `body` refuse the file by tool name.\n- MCP set_tool_holder writes the reference (holder.library in get_job);\n  add_tool refuses a definition's own holder reference, edit_tool a\n  holder patch.\n- UI: the tool settings show the entry's holder diameter and length as\n  text; the Profile tab names the entry and the picker shows it. The\n  unchanged outline keeps the reference, an edited point makes the\n  holder a custom profile.\n\nPinned for every library entry: judged tool, envelope, band stack,\nstamp term and facets equal those of the drawn copy an older build\nstored (crates/app/tests/holder_reference.rs).\n\nStacked on #2054.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: a project or tool library saved with a library holder\nstates it as a reference (project v62, .camtools version 2); v0.21.0 and\nolder refuse such a file. `ToolBody` has a new public field `library`.\n\nFixes #2016\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
